  'cr.title': 'Sources and credits', 'cr.data': 'Data snapshot taken {date}. Natural events: NASA EONET. Asteroid trajectories: NASA/JPL NHATS and Close-Approach Data. Space-weather events are documented historical events.',
  'cr.model': 'The sizing model uses first-order relations from standard references. It is built for learning trade-offs, not for flight.',
  'cr.assets': 'Moon colour and elevation (LRO), the Bennu shape model and astronaut portraits are NASA public-domain media. Earth (day, clouds, night lights), Mars, the Sun and the other planets use Solar System Scope textures (CC BY 4.0, based on NASA data); Mars is re-coloured to the NASA Viking mosaic. Planet distances in the Solar System view are true to scale; planet sizes are enlarged so they can be seen. NASA does not endorse this game. Crew members are fictional.',
  'cr.team': 'Built by team SpaceAtlas for the NASA Space Apps Challenge.',
  'crew.shared': 'What you have in common',
  'crew.solo': 'Playing solo, you run all four stations yourself. Your bonus applies to the whole mission.',
  'crew.maya.link': 'Like Mae Jemison, Maya trained as a chemical engineer at Stanford and looks at the whole mission, not a single part. That is the Systems job: cost, margins and risk.',
  'crew.dani.link': 'Like Franklin Chang-Díaz, Daniel grew up in Costa Rica and builds rocket engines. That makes him the Spacecraft lead: power, heat and propulsion.',
  'crew.rin.link': 'Like Jessica Watkins, Rin is a geologist who reads other worlds through rover and orbiter data. That puts them at the Science station: which instruments fly and what they return.',
  'crew.noor.link': 'Like Christina Koch, Noor is an electrical engineer who builds hardware that must work far from any repair shop. That puts them on Comms & Ops: launcher, orbit and the link home.',
  'crew.sofia.link': 'Like Ellen Ochoa, who researched optical systems before she flew, Sofía works on optics and instrument physics. That puts her at the Science station.',
  'crew.lucas.link': 'Like Sally Ride, who served as capsule communicator between mission control and the crew, Lucas works where the mission is run. That puts him on Comms & Ops.',
  'home.event': 'Made for the NASA Space Apps Challenge',
