  'gd.objective.q': 'What does your mission want to find out?',
  'gd.objective.l': 'Every mission starts with a science question. It decides which instruments make sense and how the result will be judged.',
  'gd.objective.short': 'Objective',
  'gd.ambition.q': 'How long will the mission work?',
  'gd.ambition.l': 'More time in operation returns more science, but the spacecraft must last longer and the ground team costs money every year.',
  'gd.ambition.short': 'Duration',
  'gd.instruments.q': 'Which instruments will the spacecraft carry?',
  'gd.instruments.l': 'Each instrument measures something different. Pick the ones that serve the objective: each adds mass, power draw and cost.',
  'gd.instruments.short': 'Instruments',
  'gd.orbit.q': 'Where will the spacecraft work?',
  'gd.orbit.l': 'The place changes everything: how much sunlight arrives, how cold it gets, how much manoeuvring it takes and what the instruments can see.',
  'gd.orbit.short': 'Orbit',
  'gd.bus.q': 'How big does the spacecraft need to be?',
  'gd.bus.l': 'The bus is the structure that carries the instruments. It must hold the payload, but every size up adds mass and cost.',
  'gd.bus.short': 'Size',
  'gd.power.q': 'Where does the power come from?',
  'gd.power.l': 'Solar panels are light and cheap but depend on the Sun. An RTG works anywhere, but it is heavy and very expensive.',
  'gd.power.short': 'Power',
  'gd.battery.q': 'How much energy should it store for the dark?',
  'gd.battery.l': 'When the spacecraft enters shadow, the panels stop. The battery has to keep everything running until the Sun returns.',
  'gd.battery.short': 'Battery',
  'gd.prop.q': 'How will the spacecraft manoeuvre?',
  'gd.prop.l': 'In space, changing speed burns propellant. Delta-v is how much the speed must change to arrive, brake and stay in place.',
  'gd.prop.short': 'Propulsion',
  'gd.antenna.q': 'How does the spacecraft talk to Earth?',
  'gd.antenna.l': 'Data that never reaches Earth is not science. Bigger antennas send more data, but weigh and cost more.',
  'gd.antenna.short': 'Comms',
  'gd.launcher.q': 'Which rocket carries your spacecraft?',
  'gd.launcher.l': 'The rocket has to take the spacecraft to its destination with room to spare. Bigger rockets carry more but cost far more.',
  'gd.launcher.short': 'Rocket',
  'gd.objective.ctx': 'Target: {target}. The mission is judged by the science it brings back: minimum goal {min} pts, full goal {full} pts.', 
  'gd.ambition.ctx': 'The ground team costs about ${team} million per year. The mission\'s total cap is ${budget} million.',
  'gd.instruments.ctx': 'Objective: {obj}. The current bus carries up to {cap} kg of instruments; you can change the size later.',
  'gd.orbit.ctx.leo': 'In low orbit, the spacecraft circles Earth every 90 to 100 minutes and spends about a third of that time in shadow.',
  'gd.orbit.ctx.moon': 'Staying in orbit is simpler. Landing takes far more manoeuvring but lets you touch the ice. At the south pole, some craters never see sunlight.',
  'gd.orbit.ctx.neo': 'A flyby uses little propellant, but the encounter lasts hours. Staying with the asteroid gives months of observation.',
  'gd.orbit.ctx.mars': 'From orbit, the spacecraft sees the whole planet. On the surface, the Martian night lasts about 12 hours and dust settles on the panels.',
  'gd.bus.ctx': 'Your instruments weigh {pay} kg in total. The bus you pick has to carry that.',
  'gd.power.ctx': 'Here the Sun delivers {flux} W per square metre ({pct}% of what reaches Earth). Your spacecraft draws about {load} W.',
  'gd.battery.ctx': 'The longest dark period lasts {hours} h. To get through it, the spacecraft needs {need} Wh stored.',
  'gd.battery.ctx0': 'This plan has no day-night cycle: the battery only covers peaks in demand.',
  'gd.prop.ctx': 'After the rocket releases it, the spacecraft still has to change its speed by {dv} m/s to arrive and stay in place.',
  'gd.prop.ctx0': 'In this plan the rocket itself drops the spacecraft in the right place. Extra manoeuvres are optional.',
  'gd.antenna.ctx': 'The signal takes {delay} to reach Earth. Your instruments produce {gen} Gb of data per day.',
  'gd.launcher.ctx': 'Your spacecraft weighs {mass} kg with propellant. The rocket\'s trip: {dest}.',
