  'part.bus.a': 'It is the chassis and body of a car.',
  'part.power.n': 'Power',
  'part.power.d': 'Solar panels turn light into electricity. An RTG turns the heat of plutonium-238 into electricity, far from the Sun or in shadow.',
  'part.power.a': 'Nothing works without power: it is the spacecraft\'s wall socket.',
  'part.battery.n': 'Battery',
  'part.battery.d': 'Stores energy for when there is no Sun: eclipses in orbit or night on the surface.',
  'part.battery.a': 'It works like a phone\'s power bank.',
  'part.thermal.n': 'Thermal control',
  'part.thermal.d': 'Heaters and radiators keep the electronics between about −20 °C and +50 °C, in cold shadow and hot sunlight.',
  'part.thermal.a': 'A coat and a fan at the same time.',
  'part.prop.n': 'Propulsion',
  'part.prop.d': 'Tanks and an engine to change speed in space: enter orbit, land, correct the course.',
  'part.prop.a': 'With no air to push on, the spacecraft moves by throwing gas backwards.',
  'part.avionics.n': 'Flight computer',
  'part.avionics.d': 'Flies the spacecraft, stores data between contacts and reacts to faults. Backup units take over if something breaks.',
  'part.avionics.a': 'The spacecraft\'s brain, with a spare brain.',
  'part.antenna.n': 'Antenna',
  'part.antenna.d': 'Sends the data and receives commands from Earth. The bigger the dish, the more focused the signal.',
  'part.antenna.a': 'A focused torch reaches further than a bare bulb.',
  'part.inst.n': 'Instruments',
  'part.inst.d': 'Cameras, spectrometers and sensors: the reason the mission exists.',
  'part.inst.a': 'The spacecraft\'s eyes and ears.',
  'part.legs.n': 'Landing legs',
  'part.legs.d': 'Absorb the touchdown and keep the spacecraft steady on the ground.',
  'part.legs.a': 'Like an aircraft\'s landing gear.',
  'part.stage1.n': 'First stage',
  'part.stage1.d': 'The most powerful engines lift the rocket off the pad and push through the thickest part of the atmosphere.',
  'part.stage1.a': 'After a few minutes, out of propellant, it separates. Some land to be reused; others fall into the ocean.',
  'part.boost.n': 'Side boosters',
  'part.boost.d': 'Solid-fuel rockets that add thrust at the start of the climb.',
  'part.boost.a': 'They burn for a minute or two, let go and fall into the ocean.',
  'part.inter.n': 'Interstage',
  'part.inter.d': 'A ring that joins the stages and shields the upper stage\'s engine.',
  'part.inter.a': 'It leaves with the lower stage.',
  'part.stage2.n': 'Upper stage',
  'part.stage2.d': 'An engine built for vacuum: it finishes accelerating the spacecraft to orbital speed (about 7.8 km/s in low orbit) or beyond.',
  'part.stage2.a': 'After releasing the spacecraft, it re-enters and burns up or moves to a disposal orbit.',
  'part.fairing.n': 'Fairing',
  'part.fairing.d': 'A shell that protects the spacecraft from air and heat during the climb.',
  'part.fairing.a': 'It splits in two halves a few minutes after launch, once the air is thin.',
  'part.payload.n': 'Your spacecraft',
  'part.payload.d': 'The payload: it rides inside the fairing, held to the last stage by an adapter.',
  'part.payload.a': 'It separates from the rocket and the mission begins.',
